var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#CFAnelastics","page":"Home","text":"Anelastic binary fluid in a 2D box, discretized with energy-consistent finite volumes on a C-grid, in the ClimFlows ecosystem. The source is at CFAnelastics.jl.","title":"CFAnelastics"},{"category":"section","location":"#The-model","page":"Home","text":"AN2D advances the tracers m = rho_R (mathrmconsvar q) at cell centers and the velocity (u w) on the faces, where rho_R(z) is a hydrostatic reference density (AnelasticReference), under the constraint nablacdot(rho_R mathbfu) = 0. The pressure varphi = (p - p_R)rho_R that enforces it is found at each evaluation of the tendencies by the PoissonSolver, with impermeable walls and periodic or bounded horizontal directions.\n\nThe forcing of the momentum is chosen by a BuoyancyScheme:\n\nscheme momentum forcing\nThermodynamicForcing -mathrmconsvarnablapi - qnablamu - nabla B - ghat z, with a horizontal part\nConsistentBuoyancy along z only, b = g(rho_R v - 1)\nLegacyBuoyancy along z only, b = g(1 - 1(rho_R v))","title":"The model"},{"category":"section","location":"#Usage","page":"Home","text":"using CFAnelastics, CFBoxes, CFDiffusionSchemes, CFTimeSchemes, ClimFluids\nusing CFPlanets: Tank2D\nusing LoopManagers: MultiThread, VectorizedCPU\n\nspace = Tank2D(Lx = 1.0, Lz = 0.5, g = 10.0)\nfluid = NonlinearBinaryFluid(:potential_temperature, (; p0 = 1e5, T0 = 280.0, q0 = 0.035, Cp0 = 4000.0, v0 = 1e-3,\n    α_T = 2e-4, α_q = 0.8, α_p = 1e-6, M_s = 3.14038218e-2, R = 8.31446261815324, α_TT = 1e-5, γ = 1e-7))\ndomain = Box2D(; Mx = 32, Mz = 16, boundary = (Periodic, Bounded))\nwall = Wall(tangential = FreeSlip(), tracers = (Flux(0.0), Flux(0.0)))\nmodel = AN2D((; mgr = MultiThread(VectorizedCPU()), domain, space, fluid,\n    spatial_scheme = Centred2(), vortex_scheme = VortexEnergyCons(), buoyancy_scheme = ThermodynamicForcing(),\n    thermoflux_scheme = ThermoFluxConsistent(k_T = 1e-4, k_q = 1e-5), viscosity_scheme = ViscosityScheme(dyn_visc = 1e-3),\n    anelastic_reference = AnelasticReference(domain, space, 1000.0; pref = 1e5),\n    boundary_conditions = BoxBoundaryConditions(domain; bottom = wall, top = wall), gauge_offset = 0.0))\n\nstate = CFAnelastics.initialize(model; consvar = (x, z) -> 280 + z / 0.5 + 0.3 * sin(2π * x), q = (x, z) -> 0.035)\nstate = CFAnelastics.loop(state, model, CFTimeSchemes.RungeKutta4(model),\n                          (; Nslice = 2, slice_size = 1.0, dt_max = 0.1, cfl = 0.8))\n\nThe tendencies are CFTimeSchemes.tendencies!(dstate, scratch, model, state, t), which returns (dstate, scratch); both are allocated when void, and the call does not allocate once they are.","title":"Usage"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"module","location":"#CFAnelastics.CFAnelastics","page":"Home","text":"CFAnelastics\n\nAnelastic binary fluid in a box: the AN2D model (AN2D), its reference state (AnelasticReference), the Poisson solver for its pressure (PoissonSolver) and its momentum forcing (BuoyancyScheme).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.CFAnelastics"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.AN2D","page":"Home","text":"model = AN2D((; mgr, domain, space, fluid, spatial_scheme, vortex_scheme, buoyancy_scheme, thermoflux_scheme,\n                viscosity_scheme, anelastic_reference, boundary_conditions, gauge_offset))\n\nAnelastic binary fluid in a 2D box (x, z): prognostic m = ρR (consvar, q) at cell centers and the velocity (u, w) on faces, with ∇·(ρR u) = 0. spatial_scheme (e.g. Centred2()) sets the interpolations and differences of the C-grid, vortex_scheme the vortex force, buoyancy_scheme the momentum forcing (see BuoyancyScheme). gauge_offset [m² s⁻²] is the constant added to the kinematic pressure φ = (p - pR)/ρR, defined up to a constant: the horizontal mean of φ on the bottom level is gauge_offset (see PoissonSolver). It changes the pressure but no tendency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.AN2D"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.AnelasticReference","page":"Home","text":"reference = AnelasticReference(domain, space, ρ; pref)\n\nReference state of the anelastic model on the grid of domain spanning space, along the full z axis (halo included): the density ρ_R and the hydrostatic pressure p_R at cell centers, with ∂pR/∂z = -g ℑz(ρR) discretely (the density of the w-face between two cells is their average, as in the model). The pressure is anchored at the height space.z0 where the geopotential vanishes: pref [Pa] is the value at z0 of the piecewise-linear interpolant of the cell-center pressures (extrapolated linearly from the two nearest interior cells if z0 is outside the box). The density ρ [kg m⁻³] is a number, a function ρ(z) of the height z above the bottom, or a vector of its values in the Mz cells, from bottom to top (extended by its end values into the halo). Face values and the specific volume are computed where needed: ρ_R on w-faces is the average of the two cells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.AnelasticReference"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.BuoyancyForce","page":"Home","text":"BuoyancyForce\n\nMomentum forcing by a buoyancy b [m s⁻²] along z only, computed at the cells and averaged to the w-faces: ConsistentBuoyancy or LegacyBuoyancy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.BuoyancyForce"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.BuoyancyScheme","page":"Home","text":"BuoyancyScheme\n\nMomentum forcing of the anelastic model by the thermodynamic state: ThermodynamicForcing, or a buoyancy force (BuoyancyForce), ConsistentBuoyancy or LegacyBuoyancy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.BuoyancyScheme"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.ComplexCoefficients","page":"Home","text":"ComplexCoefficients()\n\nLayout of the coefficients of a transformed level as soon as one horizontal direction is periodic: complex Fourier(-cosine) coefficients.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.ComplexCoefficients"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.ConsistentBuoyancy","page":"Home","text":"ConsistentBuoyancy()\n\nBuoyancy force with b = g (ρR v - 1), v the specific volume at the reference pressure pR: the energetically consistent buoyancy of Tailleux & Dubos (2024).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.ConsistentBuoyancy"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.LegacyBuoyancy","page":"Home","text":"LegacyBuoyancy()\n\nBuoyancy force with the traditional b = g (1 - 1/(ρR v)) = -g (ρ - ρR)/ρR, ρ = 1/v the density at the reference pressure pR.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.LegacyBuoyancy"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.PoissonSolver","page":"Home","text":"solver = PoissonSolver(domain, spacing, ρ_R; gauge_offset = 0, flags = FFTW.MEASURE)\n\nPoisson solver for the anelastic pressure on a Box2D or Box3D, with grid spacing (dx, dz) or (dx, dy, dz) in m. The vertical direction must be bounded; horizontal directions may be periodic or bounded, following the box topology. ρ_R (kg m⁻³) is the reference density at cell centers along the full z axis, halo included. flags are the FFTW planner flags: FFTW.MEASURE times candidate algorithms at construction and keeps the fastest, so results may differ at round-off level between runs; FFTW.ESTIMATE plans at once, reproducibly, with slower transforms. gauge_offset [m² s⁻²] is the constant added to the solved φ (see pressure!). Apply with pressure!.\n\nThe tridiagonal system of a row of modes_by_level (horizontal eigenvalue λ) at level j = 1, …, Mz (interior levels) reads\n\na_j φ_{j-1} + b_j φ_j + c_j φ_{j+1} = r_j,\na_j = ρ_w(j - 1/2) / Δz²  (0 at the bottom wall),   c_j = ρ_w(j + 1/2) / Δz²  (0 at the top wall),\nb_j = λ ρ_R(j) - a_j - c_j,\n\nand is solved by the Thomas algorithm, with pivots p1 = b1, pj = bj - aj c{j-1} / p_{j-1}:\n\nforward elimination:   y_1 = r_1 / p_1,   y_j = (r_j - a_j y_{j-1}) / p_j,\nback substitution:     φ_Mz = y_Mz,       φ_j = y_j - (c_j / p_j) φ_{j+1}.\n\nFields:\n\ndomain: the box\ninv_spacing: (1/Δx, 1/Δz) or (1/Δx, 1/Δy, 1/Δz)  [m⁻¹]\ngauge_offset: constant added to φ after the solve, the gauge of the pressure  [m² s⁻²]\nρ_R: reference density at cell centers, full z axis (halo included)  [kg m⁻³]\nρ_w: reference density on w-faces, ℑ(ρ_R), full z face axis  [kg m⁻³]\nrhs: interior cells (Mx[, My], Mz): r/scale before the forward transform, φ after the backward one\nmodes: the transform coefficients of each level, as real numbers, last dimension the level. With a periodic direction they are complex and stored with real and imaginary parts interleaved along the first dimension, of size (2 × first coefficient count, other coefficient counts…, Mz); otherwise (Mx[, My], Mz) cosine coefficients\nspectral: modes as the transforms see it: complex numbers (a reinterpretation of the same memory), or modes itself when no direction is periodic\nmodes_by_level: the same memory as modes, seen as (row, level): each row, a real or imaginary part of one coefficient, is one tridiagonal system\nforward_plan: transform of one level, rhs → spectral: r2c along the periodic directions, or DCT-II along all directions when none is periodic\nforward_cosine_plan: in place on one level of spectral: DCT-II along the bounded directions, after the r2c; nothing when no direction is bounded or none is periodic\nbackward_cosine_plan: in place, the inverse of forward_cosine_plan up to its normalization (DCT-III), or nothing\nbackward_plan: one level, spectral → rhs, the inverse of forward_plan up to its normalization: c2r (which overwrites its input), or DCT-III\nscale: backward ∘ forward = scale × identity\nsub_diagonal: a_j per level  [kg m⁻⁵]\nthomas_factor: cj / pj per (row, level)\ninv_pivot: 1 / p_j per (row, level)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.PoissonSolver"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients","page":"Home","text":"RealCoefficients()\n\nLayout of the coefficients of a transformed level when every horizontal direction is bounded: real cosine coefficients.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients"},{"category":"type","location":"#CFAnelastics.ThermodynamicForcing","page":"Home","text":"ThermodynamicForcing()\n\nMomentum forcing in thermodynamic form, -consvar ∇conjvar - q ∇chempot - ∇B - g ẑ, with B = h - conjvar consvar - chempot q the potential of the forcing, all at the reference pressure p_R; it has a horizontal component.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.ThermodynamicForcing"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.advective_flux!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"mu, mw = advective_flux!((mu, mw), model::AN2D, state)\n\nAdvective fluxes of the tracers on the faces, m u = u ℑX(m) and m w = w ℑZ(m) (third index: tracer). Periodized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.advective_flux!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.alignment_flag-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"flag = alignment_flag(F, M)\n\nFFTW.UNALIGNED for the plans that read or write an array whose levels of M numbers of type F do not all start on a 16-byte boundary, 0 otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.alignment_flag"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.anchored_pressure-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Home","text":"p = anchored_pressure(p, domain, dz, z0, pref)\n\np plus the constant such that its piecewise-linear interpolant between cell centers has the value pref at the height z0. The segment is that between two interior cells containing z0, or the nearest one (linear extrapolation) outside the box.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.anchored_pressure"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.apply_tracer_bcs!-Tuple{Any, AN2D, Any}","page":"Home","text":"apply_tracer_bcs!((consflux_x, qflux_x, consflux_z, qflux_z), model::AN2D, …)\n\nSet the fluxes of consvar and q on the wall faces from the wall conditions, replacing those computed by fluxes!: along each dimension with walls, then on each wall, then at each position along it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.apply_tracer_bcs!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.backward_transform!-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{PoissonSolver{N}, Any}} where N","page":"Home","text":"rhs = backward_transform!(solver::PoissonSolver, mgr)\n\nStep 5, for each level k: the inverse cosine transforms in place, then spectral → rhs (overwriting spectral).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.backward_transform!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.buoyancy-Tuple{LegacyBuoyancy, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"b = buoyancy(scheme::BuoyancyScheme, g, ρ_R, v)\n\nBuoyancy b [m s⁻²] at a level of reference density ρR, from the specific volume v of the fluid: g (1 - 1/(ρR v)) for LegacyBuoyancy, g (ρ_R v - 1) for ConsistentBuoyancy (and as the diagnostic buoyancy of ThermodynamicForcing).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.buoyancy"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.buoyancy_field!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"b = buoyancy_field!(b, model::AN2D, consvar, q)\n\nBuoyancy [m s⁻²] of the model's buoyancy scheme on the cells, from the specific volume v(p_R, consvar, q) (see buoyancy).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.buoyancy_field!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.cell_value-Tuple{Number, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"value = cell_value(f, k, z)\n\nValue of a profile in cell k (k = 1, …, Mz in the interior) at height z: a number, a function of z, or a vector of the Mz cell values, extended by its end values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.cell_value"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.cfl_condition-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Vararg{Any, 5}}} where F","page":"Home","text":"dt, Nperslice = cfl_condition(model::AN2D, scheme, state, cfl, slice_size, dt_max)\n\nReturn the time step dt [s] and the number Nperslice of steps per time slice: the largest dt that fits a whole number of times in slice_size [s] and is at most dt_max [s] and cfl times the stability limit of the explicit scheme (CFTimeSchemes.max_time_step) for the fastest discrete frequency max_frequency(model, state). cfl is a fraction of that limit: cfl ≤ 1 is stable for any explicit scheme.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.cfl_condition"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.check_length-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"check_length(ρ, Mz)\n\nThrow an error if the density profile ρ is a vector without one value per interior cell.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.check_length"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.check_vertical-Tuple{CFBoxes.CGrid.Bounded}","page":"Home","text":"check_vertical(topology)\n\nThrow an error unless the vertical direction is bounded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.check_vertical"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.close_outputs-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"close_outputs(outputs)\n\nClose outputs, if any, at the end of the run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.close_outputs"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.coefficient_counts-Tuple{CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"Mc = coefficient_counts(layout, horizontal, M)\n\nNumber of coefficients along each horizontal direction: M, except M÷2 + 1 along the first periodic direction, whose negative frequencies the r2c transform leaves out (they are the complex conjugates).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.coefficient_counts"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.coefficient_eigenvalues-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"λ = coefficient_eigenvalues(horizontal, M, Mc, spacing)\n\nEigenvalue of each coefficient (counts Mc): the sum over horizontal directions of horizontal_eigenvalue.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.coefficient_eigenvalues"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.cons_flux_bc-Tuple{CFBoxes.CGrid.Flux{<:Any, :density}, Vararg{Any, 6}}","page":"Home","text":"flux = cons_flux_bc(bc, value, thermo, i_cell, wall, model, qflux)\n\nFlux of consvar on a wall face: the prescribed flux F of ρ consvar (Flux), the prescribed heat flux F (HeatFlux), or the face flux with the wall value cons_w at distance d and Twall = T(pwall, consw, qcell) (Value). The wall delivers exactly the heat flux (HeatFlux, or Value with the consistent scheme): the production between the wall and the cell center is inside consflux.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.cons_flux_bc"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.copy_to_interior!-Tuple{Any, PoissonSolver{2}, Any}","page":"Home","text":"φ = copy_to_interior!(φ, solver::PoissonSolver, mgr)\n\nφ = rhs + gauge_offset on the interior cells of the halo-included φ, after solve!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.copy_to_interior!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.cosine_plans-Tuple{Any, Tuple{}, Any}","page":"Home","text":"forward_cosine, backward_cosine = cosine_plans(level, bounded, flags)\n\nIn-place DCT-II and DCT-III plans along the bounded directions of a complex level, or nothing without bounded directions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.cosine_plans"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.density!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"ρ = density!(ρ, model::AN2D)\n\nReference density ρ_R(z) [kg m⁻³] on the cells, halo included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.density!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.describe_diagnostics-Tuple{AN2D}","page":"Home","text":"describe_diagnostics(model::AN2D)\n\nPrint the name, long name and units of each diagnostic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.describe_diagnostics"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.diagnostic_info-Tuple{AN2D}","page":"Home","text":"info = diagnostic_info(model::AN2D)\n\nLong name, units and grid location of each diagnostic of diagnostics(model), as a named tuple of (; long_name, units, location).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.diagnostic_info"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.diagnostics-Union{Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}}, Tuple{F}} where F","page":"Home","text":"book = diagnostics(model::AN2D)\n\nCookBook of the AN2D diagnostics, opened with open(book; state, dstate, scratch, model). Names, long names and units: see diagnostic_info (or describe_diagnostics(model)). Debugging intermediates: internal_diagnostics.\n\nBuild the book once and reuse it: it owns the output array of each computed diagnostic, allocated on its grid location on first use, which every session of the book overwrites. The other diagnostics are the arrays (or views) of the state, tendency and scratch. Copy a result to keep it beyond the next session.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.diagnostics"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.dissipative_heating!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxConsistent, Vararg{Any, 4}}} where F","page":"Home","text":"ρε, σ_cons = dissipative_heating!((ρε, σ_cons), model::AN2D, thermoflux_scheme, state, (uτ_x, uτ_z, F_x, F_z), thermo,\n                                  (diffusive_heating_x, diffusive_heating_z))\n\nAt the interior cells: the viscous heating ρε = ∇·(u·τ) - u·F [W m⁻³], and the production of consvar σ = (ρε + ℑ(diffusive heating)) / conjvar with ThermoFluxConsistent, or σ = 0 with ThermoFluxDowngradient. Zero-gradient halo. Wall faces carry no diffusive heating (zero-gradient halo of conjvar, chempot): the energy a wall delivers is conjvarcell consflux + chempotcell qflux, see cons_flux_bc.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.dissipative_heating!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.divergence!-Tuple{Any, PoissonSolver{2}, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"rhs = divergence!(rhs, solver::PoissonSolver, mgr, dU, factor)\n\nr = ∇·(ρ dU) on the interior cells, in 2D and 3D: Σd δd(ρd dUd) / Δd, ρR(z) on horizontal faces and ρ_w on w-faces, times factor, written into rhs (interior cells only: cell i of the domain is i - H in rhs, H the halo width). Wall faces carry dU·n = 0, hence no flux.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.divergence!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.divergence_field!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"div = divergence_field!(div, model, Vx, Vz)\n\nDivergence of a vector (Vx, Vz) on the faces, at the cells: δx Vx / Δx + δz Vz / Δz on the interior cells, with a zero-gradient halo.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.divergence_field!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.divergence_free_velocity-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"(u, w) = divergence_free_velocity(model::AN2D, ψ)\n\nVelocity on the faces with discretely divergence-free mass flux, ∇·(ρR u) = 0 in every cell, from a mass streamfunction ψ(X, Z) [kg m⁻¹ s⁻¹] evaluated at the cell vertices: ρR u = δz ψ / Δz on u-faces and ρR w = -δx ψ / Δx on w-faces (ρR averaged from the two cells). The velocity through a wall vanishes where ψ is constant along it. Faces without two neighboring cells (halo edges) are zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.divergence_free_velocity"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.dm!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"dm = dm!(dm, model::AN2D, state, (mu, mw, consflux_x, consflux_z, qflux_x, qflux_z, σ_cons))\n\nTracer tendencies at the interior cells, dm = -∇·(m u) - ∇·(consflux, qflux) + (σ_cons, 0), in flux form: δx/Δx and δz/Δz of the face fluxes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.dm!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.dstate_bc!-Tuple{Any, AN2D}","page":"Home","text":"dstate = dstate_bc!(dstate, model::AN2D)\n\nSet the tendencies dstate = (; m, u, w) to zero in the halo, and the tendency of the normal velocity on the walls.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.dstate_bc!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.face_densities-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","text":"ρ_w = face_densities(ρ_R)\n\nρw on the faces J of the full z axis: ρw[J] = ℑ(ρ_R) between cells J-1 and J. The two outermost faces, beyond the halo, have no cell on one side and are left at zero (never read).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.face_densities"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.fluxes!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"consflux_x, consflux_z, qflux_x, qflux_z, diffusive_heating_x, diffusive_heating_z = fluxes!(outputs, model::AN2D, thermo)\n\nIrreversible fluxes on the faces: qflux = -ρR kq (∂q - Γ ∂pR) and consflux (carrying the heat flux -ρR Cp kT ∂T, or down the gradient of consvar, see `CFDiffusionSchemes.consvarflux), coefficients averaged from the two cells, ∂p_R = δz p_R / Δz = -g ℑz(ρ_R) on w-faces and 0 on u-faces; on wall faces, fromapplytracerbcs!`. Also the diffusive heating -(consflux ∂conjvar + qflux ∂chempot), zero on wall faces (zero-gradient halo of conjvar, chempot). Periodized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.fluxes!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.forcing_potential-Tuple{ThermodynamicForcing, Vararg{Any, 8}}","page":"Home","text":"B = forcing_potential(scheme::BuoyancyScheme, fluid, g, ρ_R, p, cons, q, conj, chem)\n\nPotential B of the momentum forcing at reference density ρ_R and pressure p: h - conjvar consvar - chempot q [J kg⁻¹] for ThermodynamicForcing, or the buoyancy b [m s⁻²], see buoyancy, for a BuoyancyForce.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.forcing_potential"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.forward_transform!-Union{Tuple{N}, Tuple{PoissonSolver{N}, Any}} where N","page":"Home","text":"spectral = forward_transform!(solver::PoissonSolver, mgr)\n\nStep 3, for each level k (the last dimension): rhs → spectral, then the cosine transforms of the bounded directions in place. Levels are contiguous in memory, so the one-level plans apply to them, and independent: they run in parallel under a threaded manager.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.forward_transform!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.horizontal_eigenvalue-Tuple{CFBoxes.CGrid.Periodic, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"λ = horizontal_eigenvalue(topology, m, M, Δ)\n\nEigenvalue of the second difference (φ{m+1} - 2φm + φ_{m-1})/Δ² for the coefficient m = 0, 1, … along one direction of M points: frequency min(m, M-m) of the Fourier transform (periodic), or the cosine mode m (bounded).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.horizontal_eigenvalue"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.horizontal_eigenvalues-Tuple{CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients, Vararg{Any, 4}}","page":"Home","text":"λ = horizontal_eigenvalues(layout, horizontal, M, Mc, spacing)\n\nEigenvalue of each row of modes_by_level: for each coefficient (counts Mc), in memory order, the sum over horizontal directions; complex coefficients have two rows, their real and imaginary parts, with the same λ. The first coefficient (all m = 0) is the horizontal mean, with λ = 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.horizontal_eigenvalues"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.horizontal_plans-Tuple{CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients, Vararg{Any, 5}}","page":"Home","text":"forward, forward_cosine, backward_cosine, backward = horizontal_plans(layout, F, horizontal, M, Mc, flags)\n\nFFTW plans transforming one level (see PoissonSolver), made on fresh arrays, which planning overwrites, and applied to the levels of rhs and spectral.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.horizontal_plans"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.hydrostatic_pressure-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"p = hydrostatic_pressure(ρ, dz, g)\n\nHydrostatic pressure at the cell centers up to an additive constant (zero in the first cell): pj - p{j-1} = -g Δz (ρ{j-1} + ρj)/2, i.e. ∂p/∂z = -g ℑz(ρ) between centers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.hydrostatic_pressure"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.increment-Tuple{Tuple{Any}, Tuple{Any}, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"increment(factors, ks, i, j)\n\nΣₙ factorₙ kₙ[i, j], accumulated in the order of n by multiply-adds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.increment"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.initial_velocity-Tuple{Any, Tuple, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"u, w = initial_velocity(F, velocity, mgr, domain)\n\nInitial velocity of initialize, in arrays of eltype F placed by the manager (see alloc): a copy of the face arrays velocity = (u, w), or zero (at rest) when velocity is nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.initial_velocity"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.initialize-Union{Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}}, Tuple{F}} where F","page":"Home","text":"state = initialize(model::AN2D; consvar, q, velocity = nothing)\n\nState (m, u, w) of the AN2D model from the tracers consvar(x, z) and q(x, z), functions of position with z = 0 at the bottom and x = 0 at the left, and the initial velocity velocity = (u, w), face arrays shaped like u and w (e.g. from divergence_free_velocity, plus a mean flow); nothing is the fluid at rest. The tracers are weighted by the reference density, m = ρ_R (consvar, q); the halo is set by the boundary conditions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.initialize"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.internal_diagnostics-Tuple{AN2D}","page":"Home","text":"book = internal_diagnostics(model::AN2D)\n\nCookBook of intermediates of the AN2D tendencies, for debugging: the vortex force ω×u = (vortexx, vortexz) of the advection, the advective fluxes of the tracers mu, mw (third index: tracer).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.internal_diagnostics"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.kinematics!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"∂u_x, ∂w_z, ∂u_z, ∂w_x, K = kinematics!((∂u_x, ∂w_z, ∂u_z, ∂w_x, K), model::AN2D, state)\n\nVelocity derivatives and kinetic energy per unit mass: at the cells ∂u/∂x = δx u / Δx, ∂w/∂z = δz w / Δz and K = (ℑx(u²) + ℑz(w²)) / 2; at the vertices ∂u/∂z = δZ u / Δz and ∂w/∂x = δX w / Δx. Periodized.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.kinematics!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.loop-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"state = loop(state, model::AN2D, time_scheme, params; outputs = nothing, book = diagnostics(model))\n\nMain time integration loop for the AN2D model; advances state in place and returns it.\n\nmodel: AN2D model instance\nstate: initial state (see initialize), overwritten by the final state; copy it first to keep it\ntime_scheme: time integration scheme\nparams: (; Nslice, slicesize, dtmax, cfl): Nslice time slices of slice_size [s], each split into equal steps of at most dt_max [s] and cfl (≤ 1 for stability) times the stability limit of time_scheme, see cfl_condition\noutputs: callable outputs(model, state, dstate, scratch, book, t), called at t = 0 and at the end of each time slice, with the diagnostics book and the time t [s]; e.g. to record diagnostics, then closed with close(outputs) when the run ends, even on error; nothing records nothing\nbook: the diagnostics CookBook handed to outputs, e.g. one with more diagnostics than diagnostics(model); built once, as each session of it overwrites the same output arrays\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.loop"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.mass_flux_x!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"flux = mass_flux_x!(flux, model::AN2D, state)\n\nMass flux ρR u [kg m⁻² s⁻¹] on the u-faces (ρR depends on z only).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.mass_flux_x!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.mass_flux_z!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"flux = mass_flux_z!(flux, model::AN2D, state)\n\nMass flux ρR w [kg m⁻² s⁻¹] on the w-faces, ρR averaged to the face. The lowest halo row of faces, without a cell below, is zero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.mass_flux_z!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.max_buoyancy_frequency-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"N = max_buoyancy_frequency(model::AN2D, m)\n\nmax(N) [s⁻¹] over the w-faces J between interior cells J-1 and J, N² = g (α ∂consvar/∂z - β ∂q/∂z), with α = ∂v/∂consvar / v and β = -∂v/∂q / v at the face (mean reference pressure, consvar and q of the two cells); N² < 0 (static instability) does not oscillate and gives 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.max_buoyancy_frequency"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.max_frequency-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"ω = max_frequency(model::AN2D, state)\n\nReturn an upper bound ω [s⁻¹] on the fastest discrete frequency of the state over the interior, the sum of:\n\nadvection, centered on the C-grid: max|u|/dx + max|w|/dz;\ndiffusion: 4 max(ν, kT, kq) (1/dx² + 1/dz²), with ν = (4μ/3) / min(ρ_R), the compressive modes being damped by (4μ/3) ∇(∇·u);\ninternal gravity waves (ω = N |kₓ|/|k| ≤ N): max(N), see max_buoyancy_frequency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.max_frequency"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.normalization-Tuple{CFBoxes.CGrid.Periodic, Any}","page":"Home","text":"factor = normalization(topology, M)\n\nFactor of backward ∘ forward along one direction of M points: M for Fourier (periodic), 2M for cosine (bounded) transforms.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.normalization"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.pointwise!-Union{Tuple{Fun}, Tuple{Any, Any, Fun, Any, Any}} where Fun","page":"Home","text":"out = pointwise!(out, mgr, f, a, b[, c])\n\nout = f(a, b[, c]) pointwise on arrays of the same grid, halo included, by the manager mgr.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.pointwise!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.pressure!-Tuple{Any, PoissonSolver, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"pressure!(φ, solver::PoissonSolver, mgr, dU)\n\nSolve for the modified pressure φ = (p - pR)/ρR (m² s⁻², cell centers, halo included) such that dU - ∇φ satisfies the discrete anelastic constraint ∇·(ρR (dU - ∇φ)) = 0 with no flow through walls, dU = (du, dw) or (du, dv, dw) being the momentum tendencies on faces (m s⁻²), periodized in periodic directions. Sets the normal components of dU on wall faces to zero. Fills the halo of φ: periodic, or zero normal gradient on walls. The horizontal mean of φ on the bottom level is `gaugeoffset(zero by default): φ is defined up to a constant, which changes no tendency. Returnsφ`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.pressure!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.pressure!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"φ = pressure!(φ, model::AN2D, (du, dw))\n\nModified pressure φ = (p - pR)/ρR [J kg⁻¹] at the cells such that ∇·(ρ_R (du - ∇φ)) = 0 with no flow through walls, by the Poisson solver of the model (see PoissonSolver). Also sets du, dw to zero on the wall faces.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.pressure!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.progress-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"progress(t_iter, slice_size, total_time)\n\nDisplay progress of the simulation in the terminal.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.progress"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.q_flux_bc-Tuple{CFBoxes.CGrid.Flux, Vararg{Any, 5}}","page":"Home","text":"flux = q_flux_bc(bc, value, thermo, i_cell, wall, model)\n\nFlux of composition on a wall face: the prescribed flux F of ρq (Flux), or the face flux with the wall value q_w at distance d from the cell center (Value).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.q_flux_bc"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.record_outputs-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Home","text":"record_outputs(outputs, model, state, dstate, scratch, book, t)\n\nCall outputs, if any, with the tendencies and scratch of state at time t (recomputed into dstate, scratch).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.record_outputs"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.solve!-Tuple{PoissonSolver, Any}","page":"Home","text":"rhs = solve!(solver::PoissonSolver, mgr)\n\nSteps 3–5: transform the levels of rhs into modes, solve the tridiagonal system of each row (see PoissonSolver), transform back into rhs. The Thomas sweeps run over the levels j, all rows at once (contiguous inner loop).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.solve!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.spectral_arrays-Tuple{CFAnelastics.RealCoefficients, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"modes, spectral = spectral_arrays(layout, F, Mc, Mz)\n\nmodes (real numbers, levels last) and its view spectral by the transforms (see PoissonSolver).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.spectral_arrays"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.spectral_layout-Tuple{Tuple{Vararg{CFBoxes.CGrid.Bounded}}}","page":"Home","text":"layout = spectral_layout(horizontal)\n\nRealCoefficients() when every horizontal direction is bounded, ComplexCoefficients() otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.spectral_layout"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.state_bc!-Tuple{Any, AN2D}","page":"Home","text":"state = state_bc!(state, model::AN2D)\n\nFill the halo of state = (; m, u, w), never its interior: the ghost velocities realize the wall conditions (see fill_velocity_halo!), and m gets a zero-gradient halo, so that the equation of state only sees valid states. The tracer fluxes through walls are set by apply_tracer_bcs!, not through the halo.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.state_bc!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.subtract_pressure_gradient!-Tuple{Any, AN2D, Any}","page":"Home","text":"du, dw = subtract_pressure_gradient!((du, dw), model::AN2D, φ)\n\nSubtract the pressure gradient, (du, dw) -= (δX φ / Δx, δZ φ / Δz), in place, with φ from pressure!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.subtract_pressure_gradient!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.thermodynamics!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"consvar, q, T, conjvar, chempot, Cp, ∂consvar_∂q, Γ, B = thermodynamics!(outputs, model::AN2D, state)\n\nPointwise thermodynamics at the reference pressure pR, from m = ρR (consvar, q), on the interior cells: consvar, q, T, conjvar, chempot, Cp, ∂consvar/∂q, Γ = -∂μ/∂p / ∂μ/∂q (barodiffusion) and B, the potential of the momentum forcing (forcing_potential). Zero-gradient halo: every difference across a wall vanishes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.thermodynamics!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.thomas_factors-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"thomas_factor, inv_pivot = thomas_factors(λ, ρ, a, c)\n\nThomas factors cj / pj and 1 / pj of every row (see PoissonSolver), with ρ the reference density of the interior levels. The rows of the mean (λ = 0: its real part, and its imaginary part, which is zero) are singular: their first equation becomes φ1 = 0 (the gauge), by setting both factors of (row, level 1) to zero, so that y1 = 0 and level 2 sees a known φ1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.thomas_factors"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.total_pressure!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"p = total_pressure!(p, model::AN2D, φ)\n\nPressure p = pR + ρR φ [Pa] on the cells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.total_pressure!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.transform_in_place!-Tuple{Nothing, Any}","page":"Home","text":"level = transform_in_place!(plan, level)\n\nApply plan to level in place, or nothing when plan is nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.transform_in_place!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.update_array!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Home","text":"x = update_array!(x, mgr, u, factors, ks)\n\nx = u + Σₙ factorₙ kₙ at every point of the 2D arrays, by the manager mgr.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.update_array!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.update_state!-Tuple{Any, AN2D, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"new = update_state!(new, model::AN2D, old, factors, increments)\n\nnew = old + Σₙ factorₙ incrementₙ for each array of the state, with the threads of the model's manager: the default update of CFTimeSchemes broadcasts on a single thread.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.update_state!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.velocity_tendencies!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, ThermodynamicForcing, Any, Any, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"du, dw = velocity_tendencies!((du, dw), model::AN2D, buoyancy_scheme, state, thermo, (K, vortex_x, vortex_z, F_x, F_z))\n\nVelocity tendencies on the faces before the pressure gradient: forcing - ∇K - ω×u + F/ρR. The forcing is -consvar ∇conjvar - q ∇chempot - ∇B - g ẑ for ThermodynamicForcing, with consvar, q = ℑ(m)/ρR on the face, or the buoyancy b = ℑZ(B) along z for a BuoyancyForce. Periodized, for pressure!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.velocity_tendencies!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.vertical_coefficients-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","text":"a, c = vertical_coefficients(ρ_w, Mz, Hz, Δz)\n\nCouplings of interior level j to the levels below (aj) and above (cj): ρ_w / Δz² through the face between them, zero through the walls (no flux). Face Hz+j is the lower face of cell Hz+j.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.vertical_coefficients"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.viscous_stress!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"uτ_x, uτ_z, F_x, F_z, wτ_xz, uτ_xz = viscous_stress!(outputs, model::AN2D, state, (∂u_x, ∂w_z, ∂u_z, ∂w_x))\n\nViscous stress for a constant dynamic viscosity μ and the Stokes hypothesis, τ = 2μ (S - (∇·u) I / 3): on the faces, the viscous force F = ∇·τ (per unit volume) and the energy flux u·τ; on the vertices, the shear-stress work ℑX(w) τxz and ℑZ(u) τxz. The dissipation ρε = ∇·(u·τ) - u·F is formed in dissipative_heating!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.viscous_stress!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFAnelastics.wall_state-Tuple{AN2D, Val{1}, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"wall = wall_state(model::AN2D, D, side, i_face, i_cell)\n\nState on a wall face normal to dimension D: (; n, d, ρ, p, ∂p), the inward normal n, the distance d to the cell center, the reference density ρ and pressure p on the face, and the gradient ∂p of the reference pressure along D (-ρ g on bottom and top walls, 0 on the others). On bottom and top walls, p is extrapolated hydrostatically from the cell.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFAnelastics.wall_state"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFTimeSchemes.tendencies!-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{Any, Any, AN2D{F, Vec, Manager, Domain, Boundary, Fluid, Spatial, Vortex, Buoyancy, ThermoFlux} where {Vec, Manager, Domain<:CFBoxes.CGrid.Box2D, Boundary<:CFBoxes.CGrid.BoxBoundaryConditions, Fluid, Spatial<:CFBoxes.CGrid.SpatialScheme, Vortex<:CFBoxes.CGrid.VortexScheme, Buoyancy<:BuoyancyScheme, ThermoFlux<:CFDiffusionSchemes.ThermoFluxScheme{F}}, Any, Any}} where F","page":"Home","text":"dstate, scratch = CFTimeSchemes.tendencies!(dstate, scratch, model::AN2D, state, t)\n\nTendencies dstate = (; m, u, w) of the AN2D model at state, and the scratch arrays of the intermediate fields, both allocated when void and overwritten otherwise. The pressure φ in scratch makes ∇·(ρ_R du) = 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFTimeSchemes.tendencies!"},{"category":"method","location":"#CFTimeSchemes.update!-Tuple{NamedTuple, AN2D, Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"new = CFTimeSchemes.update!(new, model::AN2D, old, a, ka[, b, kb[, c, kc[, d, kd]]])\n\nRunge-Kutta stage update new = old + Σₙ factorₙ incrementₙ (one to four increments) of every state array, halo included, run by the model's manager (see update_state!). A void new (non-mutating solver) keeps the default of CFTimeSchemes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"CFTimeSchemes.update!"}]
}
